        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): suppress terminal transcript gate for sessions still fresh under reset policy (fixes #106403)",
        "body": "<details>\n<summary>Additional instructions</summary>\n\n**MUST:** Keep **Allow edits from maintainers** enabled for this PR so maintainers\ncan help update the branch when needed.\n\n</details>\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where the terminal-main reconciliation gate silently resets a healthy main session on the next inbound message after idle. The gate compares transcript mtime against entry `updatedAt`, and a post-run transcript append (delivery receipt, maintenance write, tool output) creates a margin of tens of milliseconds where `mtime > updatedAt`. Once this condition is true, `freshEntry` becomes false regardless of the configured reset policy — even with a 365-day idle window. The user's session \"wakes up blank\" with no log line and no error.\n\nConcrete scenario: session completes normally (`status: \"done\"`, `endedAt` set), a delivery note touches the transcript file 93 ms after `updatedAt` is written, and the next inbound message rolls the session over. Observed on three consecutive days after idle periods.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe terminal-main transcript gate (`hasTerminalMainSessionTranscriptNewerThanRegistry`) exists to detect zombie sessions whose transcript was modified after the registry marked them done. But the gate fired for sessions still fresh under the configured reset policy — a false positive.\n\nThe fix: only honor the gate when the session is already stale under the reset policy. If the entry is still fresh (within the idle/daily window), a touched transcript is not a zombie — the session is healthy and should not be rolled over.\n\nTwo call sites patched:\n- `src/auto-reply/reply/session.ts` — `freshEntry` computation for the auto-reply admission path\n- `src/agents/command/session.ts` — `fresh` computation for the command/CLI resolve-session path\n\nThe logic is symmetric: compute policy freshness first, then apply the terminal gate only when the result is already `!fresh`. When `policyFresh` is true, the gate is a no-op (the session survives).\n\n## User Impact\n\nSessions with long idle windows (hours to days) no longer silently reset after a post-run transcript touch. The first message after idle preserves the existing session context. Sessions genuinely expired under the reset policy continue to roll over normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `src/auto-reply/reply/session.ts` — `freshEntry` now guards `terminalMainTranscriptNewerThanRegistry` with `entryFreshness?.fresh !== true`\n- `src/agents/command/session.ts` — restructured `fresh` computation to separate policy freshness from the terminal transcript gate; the gate only takes effect when the session is already stale by policy\n- `src/agents/command/session.provider-owned-reset.test.ts` — two new regression cases: a fresh session (5 min old, 30-min idle policy) with `terminalTranscriptNewer=true` is kept alive; a stale session (60 min old, 30-min idle policy) with `terminalTranscriptNewer=true` is rotated\n\n```\n$ pnpm test src/agents/command/session.provider-owned-reset.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  5 passed (5)\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/issue-106403-terminal-transcript-gate",
